12
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
Summer Rental is a 1985 American comedy film directed by Carl Reiner, written by Mark Reisman and Jeremy Stevens, and starring John Candy and Richard Crenna with supporting roles by Rip Torn, Karen Austin, Kerri
Green, John Larroquette, Joey Lawrence, Aubrey Jene, Dick Anthony Williams, Richard Herd, Carmine Caridi, Lois Hamilton, Frank McCarthy, Santos Morales, Pierrino Mascarino, Harry Yorku, and Bob Wells.

13
01:02:50,000 --> 01:02:56,000
It tells the story of an overworked air traffic controller who is put on a five weeks' paid leave and takes his family to the fictional
resort town of Citrus Cove, Florida as he experiences hilarious mishaps and contends with an arrogant sailing champion.

14
01:07:40,000 --> 01:07:46,000
An original music score was composed for the film by Alan Silvestri.

15
01:12:30,000 --> 01:12:36,000
The film was released on August 9, 1985, by Paramount Pictures.

16
01:17:20,000 --> 01:17:26,000
The film explores themes of rivalry, family vacation,
suffering parent, time off, run down house.

17
01:22:10,000 --> 01:22:16,000
The tone is lighthearted.
